desc:'Grammar that wins board marks: tenses, voice, narration, vocabulary, translation and comprehension.',
icon:'📝', chapters:[
{id:'c10-eng-ch7', title:'Comprehension', urdu:'تفہیم', comingSoon:false, lessons:[
{id:'c10-eng-ch7-l1', title:'How to Attempt a Passage', html:`<h3>Five-step method</h3><ol><li><strong>Read the questions first</strong> — so you know what to hunt for.</li><li><strong>Read the passage twice</strong> — first for the gist, second for details. Underline key lines.</li><li><strong>Answer in your own words</strong> — copying whole lines loses marks.</li><li>Keep answers <strong>short and to the point</strong> (usually 1–3 lines).</li><li>For vocabulary questions, use the <strong>context</strong> around the word.</li></ol><h3>Finding the main idea</h3><p>Ask: "What is this paragraph <em>mostly</em> about?" The answer is often in the <strong>first or last sentence</strong>. Ignore examples and details when choosing the main idea.</p>`},
{id:'c10-eng-ch7-l2', title:'Answering Short Questions', html:`<h3>Question types and how to handle them</h3><ul><li><strong>Factual (who/what/when):</strong> lift the fact, rephrase briefly.</li><li><strong>Why/how:</strong> give the reason in one clear sentence.</li><li><strong>Give the meaning of…:</strong> a synonym or short explanation — <em>e.g. "frugal" means thrifty</em>.</li><li><strong>True/False + justification:</strong> quote or paraphrase the line that proves it.</li></ul><h3>Sample</h3><p><em>Passage line: "The Indus dolphin, blind and endangered, survives only in a stretch of the Indus in Sindh."</em></p><p>Q: Where does the Indus dolphin live? → <strong>In a stretch of the River Indus in Sindh.</strong></p><p>Q: Give the meaning of "endangered". → <strong>At risk of extinction.</strong></p><p><strong>Exam tip:</strong> Match the question word — "where" needs a place, "why" needs a reason.</p>`},
{id:'c10-eng-ch7-l3', title:'Summary and Title Writing', html:`<h3>Writing a summary</h3><ul><li>Read fully, then list the <strong>main points only</strong> — drop examples, repetitions and minor details.</li><li>Write in <strong>your own words</strong>, in continuous prose (no bullets).</li><li>Keep to about <strong>one-third</strong> the original length.</li><li>Don't add opinions or new information.</li></ul><h3>Giving a title</h3><p>A good title is <strong>short</strong> (2–5 words), captures the <strong>central theme</strong>, and is not a full sentence: <em>"The Blind Dolphin"</em>, <em>"Water — Our Lifeline"</em>, <em>"The Value of Time"</em>.</p><h3>Final checklist</h3><ul><li>All questions attempted? Grammar correct? Spelling checked?</li><li>Own words used, not copied lines?</li></ul>`}
], quiz:[
{q:'The first step in attempting comprehension should be:', options:['Read the passage','Read the questions first','Write the summary','Give a title'], answer:1, explain:'Knowing the questions focuses your reading.'},
{q:'Answers should be written:', options:['Copied word-for-word','In your own words','In Urdu','As single words only'], answer:1, explain:'Rephrasing earns full marks; copying loses them.'},
{q:'The main idea is often found in the:', options:['Middle sentence','First or last sentence','Footnotes','Title only'], answer:1, explain:'Topic sentences usually open or close a paragraph.'},
{q:'A summary should be about ___ the original length:', options:['The same as','One-third of','Twice','Half exactly'], answer:1, explain:'Summaries condense to roughly one-third.'},
{q:'A good title is:', options:['A full sentence','Short and theme-capturing','Very long','A question always'], answer:1, explain:'2–5 words capturing the central theme.'},
{q:'For "Give the meaning of frugal", the best answer is:', options:['Wasteful','Thrifty','Rich','Poor'], answer:1, explain:'Frugal means thrifty/economical.'},
{q:'True/False questions need:', options:['No proof','Justification from the passage','Long essays','Guessing'], answer:1, explain:'Quote or paraphrase the proving line.'},
{q:'"Why" questions require:', options:['A place','A reason','A date','A name'], answer:1, explain:'Match the answer type to the question word.'},
{q:'In a summary you should NOT:', options:['Use own words','Add personal opinions','Drop examples','Keep it brief'], answer:1, explain:'No new ideas or opinions in a summary.'},
{q:'Reading the passage twice helps you get the:', options:['Spelling','Gist first, then details','Title only','Word count'], answer:1, explain:'First read: overall meaning; second: specifics.'}
]}]
